## 13. Forks

You may create forks of the Software.

You may modify the code and give your fork a different name.

You may commercially distribute your fork.

However, you must preserve the original copyright and attribution information.

You must not represent your fork as the official version of the Original Project without authorization.

This section specifically permits forking. You can create a fork, modify it, rename it, and commercially distribute it. However, you must preserve the original copyright and attribution information, and you cannot represent your fork as the official version of the Original Project without authorization. This balances the freedom to fork with the need to protect the original project's identity.

