## 14. Project Names and Branding

Copyright permission does not grant permission to use the Original Project's branding.

The following remain the property of their respective owners:

1. Project names.
2. Company names.
3. Product names.
4. Logos.
5. Symbols.
6. Brand identities.
7. Domain names.
8. Service marks.
9. Trademarks.

Use of the Software does not grant ownership or licensing rights to these assets.

This section makes an important distinction between copyright and trademark. A copyright license allows you to use and modify the code, but it does not give you permission to use the project's branding. Project names, company names, product names, logos, symbols, brand identities, domain names, service marks, and trademarks remain the property of their respective owners. This means you cannot use the original project's name or logo for your own product just because you used the code.

