Unless a separate written agreement states otherwise, contributors retain copyright in their original contributions.

Contributors must not knowingly submit material they do not have the legal right to contribute.

Existing contributor attribution must not be removed or falsified.

By submitting a contribution to the Project, the contributor grants the Project maintainer the permissions reasonably necessary to use, modify, reproduce, distribute, and incorporate the contribution into the Project.

This section governs contributions. Contributors retain copyright in their original contributions unless a separate written agreement says otherwise. Contributors must not submit material they do not have the legal right to contribute. Existing contributor attribution must not be removed or falsified. By submitting a contribution, the contributor grants the Project maintainer the permissions reasonably necessary to use, modify, reproduce, distribute, and incorporate the contribution into the Project. This ensures the project can continue to operate while respecting contributor rights.

